   "props": {
    "id": "CustomHtml-7",
    "html": "<style>\n.letters__frame { position: relative; max-width: 58rem; }\n.letters__word,\n.letters__stage {\n  margin: 0;\n  font-family: var(--display);\n  font-weight: 800;\n  font-stretch: 72%;\n  font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 1.4rem + 6.4vw, 6rem);\n  line-height: 0.95;\n  letter-spacing: -0.005em;\n  text-transform: uppercase;\n  color: var(--ink);\n}\n.letters__word { position: relative; }\n/* The measuring copy: the next phrase is set here, invisibly, in real text\n   flow, and each glyph's box is read off it. The visible glyphs then travel\n   to those boxes. */\n.letters__stage { position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; top: 0; visibility: hidden; pointer-events: none; }\n.letters__w { display: inline-block; white-space: nowrap; }\n.letters__g { display: inline-block; }\n.letters__word .letters__g { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; transform-origin: 50% 60%; }\n.letters__word .letters__g.is-flying { z-index: 2; will-change: transform; }\n/* A mark that is not one of the thirteen letters (the apostrophe in IT'S)\n   is parked out of sight until its phrase lands, then fades in. */\n.letters__word .letters__g--x { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 0.4s ease; }\n.letters--live .letters__word { cursor: pointer; }\n/* The press line: a brass rule that draws under the name when the letters\n   come home, and clears when they leave. Transform only. */\n.letters__rule {\n  position: absolute; left: 0; height: 2px; width: 0;\n  background: var(--brass);\n  transform-origin: 0 50%;\n  transform: scaleX(0);\n  transition: transform 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);\n}\n.letters__rule.is-on { transform: scaleX(1); }\n@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {\n  .letters__rule { transition: none; }\n}\n</style>\n<section class=\"section section--ruled letters\" aria-label=\"The letters of the name\">\n  <div class=\"wrap\">\n    <div class=\"letters__frame\">\n      <p class=\"letters__word\" data-letters>Signet Artists</p>\n      <span class=\"letters__rule\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></span>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</section>\n<script>\n(function () {\n  'use strict';\n  var doc = document;\n  var block = doc.querySelector('[data-letters]');\n  if (!block || !('animate' in Element.prototype) || !('IntersectionObserver' in window)) { return; }\n\n  /* Daniel's list, 2026-10-10, in his order. The name first and the name\n     is where the cycle returns. */\n  var PHRASES = [\n    'SIGNET ARTISTS',\n    'TASTIEST GRINS',\n    'NASTIEST GRITS',\n    'A SETTING STIRS',\n    \"IT'S AGENTS STIR\",\n    'IT TARGETS SINS',\n    'ARTISTES STING',\n    'STARTS IGNITES',\n    'ATTESTING SIRS',\n    'STRATEGISTS IN'\n  ];\n  var HOLD = 2600, HOLD_NAME = 4200, STAGGER = 42;\n\n  var section = block.closest('.letters');\n  var frame = block.parentNode;\n  var rule = frame.querySelector('.letters__rule');\n  var reduce = window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');\n\n  /* The glyph pool is the name's own letters; every phrase is a permutation\n     of them, which is the whole point and is checked here so a typo in the\n     list fails loud in the console rather than quietly dropping a letter.\n     Anything that is not a letter (the apostrophe) is an extra glyph. */\n  function lettersOf(p) { return p.toUpperCase().replace(/[^A-Z]/g, ''); }\n  var pool = lettersOf(PHRASES[0]).split('');\n  var key = pool.slice().sort().join('');\n  PHRASES = PHRASES.map(function (p) { return p.toUpperCase(); }).filter(function (p) {\n    var ok = lettersOf(p).split('').sort().join('') === key;\n    if (!ok) { console.warn('letters: \"' + p + '\" is not an anagram of \"' + PHRASES[0] + '\"'); }\n    return ok;\n  });\n  var extraCount = {};\n  PHRASES.forEach(function (p) {\n    var c = {};\n    p.replace(/[A-Z\\s]/g, '').split('').forEach(function (ch) { c[ch] = (c[ch] || 0) + 1; });\n    Object.keys(c).forEach(function (ch) { extraCount[ch] = Math.max(extraCount[ch] || 0, c[ch]); });\n  });\n\n  var stage = doc.createElement('p');\n  stage.className = 'letters__stage';\n  stage.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');\n  frame.insertBefore(stage, block);\n\n  var sr = doc.createElement('span');\n  sr.className = 'visually-hidden';\n  sr.textContent = block.textContent.trim();\n  var layer = doc.createElement('span');\n  layer.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');\n  function makeGlyph(ch, extra) {\n    var el = doc.createElement('span');\n    el.className = 'letters__g' + (extra ? ' letters__g--x' : '');\n    el.textContent = ch;\n    layer.appendChild(el);\n    return { ch: ch, el: el, x: 0, y: 0, extra: extra, parked: extra };\n  }\n  var glyphs = pool.map(function (ch) { return makeGlyph(ch, false); });\n  Object.keys(extraCount).forEach(function (ch) {\n    for (var n = 0; n < extraCount[ch]; n++) { glyphs.push(makeGlyph(ch, true)); }\n  });\n\n  var layouts = [], H = 0, nameW = 0, nameH = 0, fontPx = 48;\n\n  function measure(phrase) {\n    stage.textContent = '';\n    var slots = [];\n    phrase.split(' ').forEach(function (w, wi) {\n      if (wi) { stage.appendChild(doc.createTextNode(' ')); }\n      var word = doc.createElement('span');\n      word.className = 'letters__w';\n      w.split('').forEach(function (ch) {\n        var g = doc.createElement('span');\n        g.className = 'letters__g';\n        g.textContent = ch;\n        word.appendChild(g);\n        slots.push({ ch: ch, el: g });\n      });\n      stage.appendChild(word);\n    });\n    var box = stage.getBoundingClientRect();\n    var right = 0;\n    var out = slots.map(function (s) {\n      var r = s.el.getBoundingClientRect();\n      right = Math.max(right, r.right - box.left);\n      return { ch: s.ch, x: r.left - box.left, y: r.top - box.top };\n    });\n    return { slots: out, h: box.height, w: right };\n  }\n\n  function layoutAll() {\n    fontPx = parseFloat(getComputedStyle(block).fontSize) || fontPx;\n    layouts = PHRASES.map(measure);\n    H = 0;\n    layouts.forEach(function (l) { H = Math.max(H, l.h); });\n    nameW = layouts[0].w;\n    nameH = layouts[0].h;\n    block.style.height = H + 'px';\n    var ruleTop = nameH + Math.round(fontPx * 0.22);\n    rule.style.width = nameW + 'px';\n    rule.style.top = ruleTop + 'px';\n    /* The frame holds the rule when the name is the shortest layout. */\n    frame.style.paddingBottom = Math.max(0, ruleTop + 2 - H) + 'px';\n    stage.textContent = '';\n  }\n\n  /* Pair each glyph with a slot of the same character in reading order on\n     both sides, which keeps the paths from crossing and the travel short.\n     An extra glyph with no slot in this phrase is parked. */\n  function plan(L) {\n    var free = {};\n    L.slots.forEach(function (s, i) { (free[s.ch] = free[s.ch] || []).push(i); });\n    var moves = [], parks = [];\n    glyphs.slice().sort(function (a, b) { return (a.y - b.y) || (a.x - b.x); }).forEach(function (g) {\n      var list = free[g.ch];\n      if (list && list.length) {\n        var i = list.shift();\n        moves.push({ g: g, x: L.slots[i].x, y: L.slots[i].y });\n      } else if (g.extra) {\n        parks.push(g);\n      }\n    });\n    moves.sort(function (a, b) { return (a.y - b.y) || (a.x - b.x); });\n    return { moves: moves, parks: parks };\n  }\n\n  function place(g, x, y) {\n    g.x = x; g.y = y;\n    g.el.style.transform = 'translate(' + x + 'px, ' + y + 'px)';\n  }\n\n  var ink = '', brass = '';\n  function colours() {\n    ink = getComputedStyle(block).color;\n    var cs = getComputedStyle(doc.documentElement);\n    brass = (cs.getPropertyValue('--brass-bright') || '').trim() || ink;\n  }\n\n  /* An arc from the current box to the next: a quadratic curve lifted above\n     the straight line, sampled into keyframes, eased as one. Long trips rise\n     more. A small tilt in the direction of travel, straight on landing. */\n  function fly(g, tx, ty, delay) {\n    var dx = tx - g.x, dy = ty - g.y;\n    var dist = Math.sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);\n    var lift = -(Math.min(fontPx * 0.62, dist * 0.3) + fontPx * 0.1);\n    var cx = g.x + dx / 2, cy = g.y + dy / 2 + lift;\n    var tilt = dx > 0 ? 2.2 : (dx < 0 ? -2.2 : 0);\n    var frames = [];\n    var N = 10;\n    for (var i = 0; i <= N; i++) {\n      var t = i / N, u = 1 - t;\n      var x = u * u * g.x + 2 * u * t * cx + t * t * tx;\n      var y = u * u * g.y + 2 * u * t * cy + t * t * ty;\n      var s = 1 + 0.07 * Math.sin(Math.PI * t);\n      var r = tilt * Math.sin(Math.PI * t);\n      frames.push({\n        transform: 'translate(' + x + 'px, ' + y + 'px) scale(' + s + ') rotate(' + r + 'deg)',\n        color: t > 0.25 && t < 0.75 ? brass : ink\n      });\n    }\n    var dur = 720 + Math.min(560, dist * 0.9);\n    g.el.classList.add('is-flying');\n    var a = g.el.animate(frames, { duration: dur, delay: delay, easing: 'cubic-bezier(0.22, 0, 0.08, 1)', fill: 'forwards' });\n    a.onfinish = function () { place(g, tx, ty); a.cancel(); g.el.classList.remove('is-flying'); };\n    g.x = tx; g.y = ty;\n    return delay + dur;\n  }\n\n  var idx = 0, timer = 0, inView = false;\n\n  function go(j, instant) {\n    idx = j;\n    var p = plan(layouts[j]);\n    var end = 0, k = 0, appear = [];\n    rule.classList.remove('is-on');\n    p.parks.forEach(function (g) {\n      if (!g.parked) { g.parked = true; g.el.style.opacity = '0'; }\n    });\n    p.moves.forEach(function (m) {\n      var g = m.g;\n      if (g.extra && g.parked) { place(g, m.x, m.y); g.parked = false; appear.push(g); return; }\n      if (instant || (Math.abs(m.x - g.x) < 0.5 && Math.abs(m.y - g.y) < 0.5)) { place(g, m.x, m.y); return; }\n      end = Math.max(end, fly(g, m.x, m.y, k * STAGGER));\n      k++;\n    });\n    appear.forEach(function (g) {\n      if (instant) { g.el.style.opacity = '1'; return; }\n      setTimeout(function () { if (!g.parked) { g.el.style.opacity = '1'; } }, Math.max(0, end - 350));\n    });\n    if (j === 0) {\n      if (instant) { rule.classList.add('is-on'); }\n      else { setTimeout(function () { if (idx === 0) { rule.classList.add('is-on'); } }, Math.max(0, end - 200)); }\n    }\n    return end;\n  }\n\n  function schedule(after) {\n    clearTimeout(timer);\n    if (!inView || reduce.matches || doc.hidden) { return; }\n    timer = setTimeout(next, (after || 0) + (idx === 0 ? HOLD_NAME : HOLD));\n  }\n\n  function next() {\n    var travel = go((idx + 1) % PHRASES.length, reduce.matches);\n    schedule(travel);\n  }\n\n  function init() {\n    colours();\n    layoutAll();\n    block.textContent = '';\n    block.appendChild(sr);\n    block.appendChild(layer);\n    section.classList.add('letters--live');\n    go(0, true);\n\n    block.addEventListener('click', function () { clearTimeout(timer); next(); });\n\n    new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {\n      inView = entries[0].isIntersecting;\n      if (inView) { schedule(); } else { clearTimeout(timer); }\n    }, { threshold: 0.35 }).observe(section);\n\n    doc.addEventListener('visibilitychange', function () { if (doc.hidden) { clearTimeout(timer); } else { schedule(); } });\n    if (reduce.addEventListener) { reduce.addEventListener('change', function () { schedule(); }); }\n\n    var rt = 0;\n    window.addEventListener('resize', function () {\n      clearTimeout(rt);\n      rt = setTimeout(function () { colours(); layoutAll(); go(idx, true); }, 120);\n    });\n  }\n\n  if (doc.fonts && doc.fonts.ready) { doc.fonts.ready.then(init); } else { init(); }\n})();\n</script>",
    "_notes": "The letters of the name, 2026-10-10. The page argues from the name, and\n     this is the name taken apart: the same thirteen letters set into the\n     phrases Daniel picked from the anagram list, in his order, then put back.\n     One element per letter in the site's display type; each phrase is\n     measured in real text flow so it wraps where text wraps, and the letters\n     travel to those boxes along a lifted arc, brass in flight and ink on\n     landing. When they come home to the name a brass line draws under it.\n     Nothing else: no eyebrow, no caption, no control. His call, 2026-10-10:\n     \"kill the thirteen letters shit. no note below either.\"\n\n     Runs while in view and stands still under reduced motion. No pause\n     under the pointer: there was one, and it read as the thing not working\n     (2026-10-10, \"why paused on hover. seems weird\"). Without JS the name is plain text. Clicking the word\n     advances it; that is a nudge, not a control, so nothing is labelled.\n     Page-scoped rules, every class prefixed letters-. No library.",
    "_file": "02b-letters.html"
   }
